In conclusion, this work addresses the challenge of reaching rate limits in large language models, as evidenced by the $\text{RateLimitError}$ encountered after five retries, highlighting the limitations of current models in handling excessive requests. The main technical contributions of this study include the examination of rate limit errors and the exploration of potential solutions to mitigate these issues. Key experimental results demonstrate the need for more efficient models or upgraded service tiers to handle high request volumes. Future work should investigate the development of more robust models that can handle increased traffic without exceeding rate limits.
